It is Saturday evening in Berlin.
In Mexico, it is only early afternoon.
So not much has happened there yet today.
I am calling my family on the mobile phone.
We are doing a video call.
My mother is telling me something, but her picture keeps freezing.
The internet connection is very bad.
"Mom, please close the other apps," I say.
"And please go closer to the router."
The picture is moving slowly again.
"Try it again now," I say to her.
Usually that is all it takes.
And so it is today.
Suddenly the picture is completely sharp again.
My mother looks delighted.
She laughs and just continues speaking mid-sentence.
Finally we can converse properly.
